$y' > 0$ then $y' < 0$ about $x = -2$, so the curve rises to the maximum $(-2, 16)$ and then falls.
$y' < 0$ then $y' > 0$ about $x = 2$, so the curve falls to the minimum $(2, -16)$ and then rises.
$y''$ changes sign at $x = 0$, so the curve is concave down to the left of the origin and concave up to the right, giving a point of inflection at $(0, 0)$.

